u$ and $K_{\lambda\lambda}=1$; with rows and columns ordered by a linear extension of dominance from smaller to larger, $(K_{\lambda
u})_{\lambda,
u\in\Lambda^{+}(d,n)}$ is lower unitriangular over $\mathbb Z$, hence invertible over $\mathbb Z$.

[F3] Grothendieck group and multiplicities ([[def-grothendieck-group-of-an-essentially-small-abelian-category]], [[thm-jordan-holder-theorem-for-modules]]): $[Y]=[X]+[Z]$ for every short exact sequence $0	o X	o Y	o Z	o0$ of finite-dimensional $S$-modules, and $[N]=\sum_{\mu}[N:L^{\mu}][L^{\mu}]$ in $G_0(S	ext{-mod})$, where the composition multiplicity $[N:L^{\mu}]$ is well defined.



